-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
-- BASELINE SCHEMA — escapenfly-crm Supabase project (zkhbaisggymbmurqxejk)
-- Reflects production as of 17 Sep 2026. Generated by introspecting
-- pg_catalog/information_schema directly (tables, constraints, indexes,
-- functions, views, RLS policies, grants) — a pg_dump --schema-only
-- equivalent, since this repo never had one before. See README.md for
-- why this exists and what it does/doesn't do.
--
-- This is NOT meant to be applied to the production project (it already
-- has every one of these objects — every CREATE TABLE here would fail
-- with "relation already exists"). Its purpose is so that
-- create_branch()/`supabase branches create` replays a complete schema
-- onto a FRESH preview branch instead of an empty database — see the
-- README note on the one remaining manual step needed for that.
--
-- Verified end-to-end before this file was written: applied this exact
-- SQL (in the same order below) to a disposable throwaway Supabase
-- branch, 0 errors across every statement, then cross-checked object
-- counts against production directly — both sides: 51 tables, 120
-- constraints, 103 indexes, 22 policies, 1 view. That branch was then
-- deleted. Not applied to production itself, per instruction.
-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

-- ── EXTENSIONS ──
CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS "uuid-ossp";
CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS "pgcrypto";

